T* (OPINION OF THE COURT) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (AMBRO, Circuit Judge:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The primary issues presented in this appeal from the) Tj
T* (District Court's order denying preliminary injunctive relief) Tj
T* (are whether the Free Speech and Free Exercise Clauses of) Tj
T* (the First Amendment allow the Borough of Tenafly, New) Tj
T* (Jersey, which has permitted various secularly motivated) Tj
T* (violations of a facially neutral ordinance, to invoke that) Tj
T* (ordinance against comparable religiously motivated acts by) Tj
T* (Orthodox Jews. Because there is no evidence that the acts) Tj
T* (in question are expressive, we hold that the Free Speech) Tj
T* (Clause does not apply. We further hold, however, that the) Tj
T* (Borough's selective enforcement of its ordinance likely) Tj
T* (violated the Free Exercise Clause. Because the other) Tj
T* (requirements for injunctive relief are satisfied, we reverse) Tj
T* (and direct the District Court to issue a preliminary) Tj
T* (injunction.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I. Background) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (An ordinance in the Borough of Tenafly, which) Tj
T* (encompasses 4.4 square miles and has a population of ) Tj
T* (13,806,1 provides in pertinent part: "No person shall place) Tj
T* (any sign or advertisement, or other matter upon any pole,) Tj
T* (tree, curbstone, sidewalk or elsewhere, in any public street) Tj
T* (or public place, excepting such as may be authorized by) Tj
T* (this or any other ordinance of the Borough." Tenafly, N.J.,) Tj
T* (Ordinance 691 Article VIII\(7\) \(1954\).2  Although Ordinance) Tj
T* (691 does not allow Borough officials to make exceptions on) Tj
T* (a case-by-case basis, in practice they have often done so.) Tj
T* (House number signs nailed to utility poles in plain view are) Tj
T* (_________________________________________________________________) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. See Borough of Tenafly, About Tenafly, at http://www.tenaflynj.org/) Tj
T* (about.htm \(last visited September 20, 2002\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. Our description of the facts is based on our independent review of the) Tj
T* (record because, as explained in more detail below, the First Amendment) Tj
T* (bars us from deferring to the District Court's factual findings unless they) Tj
T* (involve witness credibility. See Hurley v. Irish-American Gay, Lesbian &) Tj
T* (Bisexual Group of Boston, 515 U.S. 557, 567 \(1995\).) Tj
