T* (Borough's property.7 In April 2000, the plaintiffs asked) Tj
T* (Verizon for permission to attach lechis to its utility poles.) Tj
T* (The plaintiffs said in a sworn statement, which the District) Tj
T* (Court found "credible," that they did not believe any) Tj
T* (municipal ordinance prohibited them from doing so, and) Tj
T* (thus that they did not need the Council's permission. Id. at) Tj
T* (155. After the plaintiffs informed Verizon about the) Tj
T* (proclamation, they say, the company's in-house counsel) Tj
T* (researched whether municipal approval was required and) Tj
T* (advised the plaintiffs that it was not.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In June 2000 Cablevision, holder of the local cable) Tj
T* (television franchise, volunteered to help the plaintiffs affix) Tj
T* (lechis to Verizon's utility poles as a community service.) Tj
T* (With the help of Cablevision personnel and equipment, an) Tj
T* (_________________________________________________________________) Tj
T* () Tj
