T* (                                7) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (eruv was completed in Tenafly sometime in September 2000.8) Tj
T* (The plaintiffs represent, and the Borough does not disagree,) Tj
T* (that only private funds have supported the eruv  and that) Tj
T* (no municipal assistance of any kind will be needed to) Tj
T* (maintain it.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Borough officials apparently did not learn that an eruv) Tj
T* (was being erected in Tenafly until late August 2000. Mayor) Tj
T* (Moscovitz and Councilman Charles Lipson met with two) Tj
T* (local Jewish leaders on September 14, 2000, to discuss the) Tj
T* (matter. One of the Jewish leaders perceived some of the) Tj
T* (Mayor's remarks as derogatory toward Orthodox Jews, and) Tj
T* (the meeting was unproductive. Twelve days later, Borough) Tj
T* (Administrator Joseph DiGiacomo, acting at the Mayor's) Tj
T* (behest, asked Cablevision why it helped attach the lechis) Tj
T* (without the Borough's permission. According to DiGiacomo,) Tj
T* (the company told him that "a Rabbi" had advised it that) Tj
T* (TEAI had the necessary government approval. Id. at 158.) Tj
T* (On October 10, 2000, Mayor Moscovitz and the Council) Tj
T* (directed the Borough Administrator to ask Cablevision to) Tj
T* (remove the lechis from the utility poles"as soon as) Tj
T* (possible." Id.) Tj
