T* () Tj
T* (A. The Free Speech Claim) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The First Amendment's Free Speech Clause provides that) Tj
T* ("Congress shall make no law . . . abridging the freedom of) Tj
T* (speech." U.S. Const. amend. I. "Speech" is not construed) Tj
T* (literally, or even limited to the use of words. Constitutional) Tj
T* (protection is afforded not only to speaking and writing, but) Tj
T* (also to some nonverbal acts of communication, viz.,) Tj
T* ("expressive conduct" \(or "symbolic speech"\). Affixing lechis) Tj
T* (to utility poles does not involve the use of words, so the) Tj
T* (plaintiffs' behavior is protected by the Free Speech Clause) Tj
T* (only if it constitutes expressive conduct.15) Tj
T* (_________________________________________________________________) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (jurisdiction to consider it. See Growth Horizons, Inc. v. Delaware County,) Tj
T* (983 F.2d 1277, 1280-84 \(3d Cir. 1993\) \(holding that district court's) Tj
T* (determination that defendant did not "make unavailable or deny") Tj
T* (housing under S 3604\(f\) was "a judgment on the merits rather than a) Tj
T* (jurisdictional decision" because the plaintiff's claim, though ultimately) Tj
T* (unsuccessful, was not frivolous\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (14. Citing Elber v. City of Newark, 256 A.2d 44 \(N.J. 1969\), the plaintiffs) Tj
T* (attempt to raise a claim under New Jersey law. Presumably because the) Tj
T* (plaintiffs did not include this claim in their complaint, the District Court) Tj
T* (did not discuss it. We shall do likewise.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (15. The Borough failed to contend in its brief that the act of affixing) Tj
T* (lechis to utility poles is not "speech" within the meaning of the First) Tj
T* (Amendment. Ordinarily we avoid addressing issues not raised in a) Tj
T* (party's opening brief. See, e.g., Kirschbaum v. WRGSB Associates, 243) Tj
T* (F.3d 145, 151 n.1 \(3d Cir. 2001\). However, "[w]hen an issue or claim is) Tj
T* (properly before the court, the court is not limited to the particular legal) Tj
T* (theories advanced by the parties, but rather retains the independent) Tj
T* (power to identify and apply the proper construction of governing law.") Tj
T* (Kamen v. Kemper Fin. Servs., Inc., 500 U.S. 90, 99 \(1991\). Thus we "may) Tj
T* (consider an issue `antecedent to . . . and ultimately dispositive of ' the) Tj
T* (dispute before [us], even an issue the parties fail to identify and brief.") Tj
T* (United Nat'l Bank v. Indep. Ins. Agents, 508 U.S. 439, 447 \(1993\)) Tj
